{"title":"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the complete factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/2/e927c09736da9f2fb3f000324613f5bef0737dc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x^3+3x^2-32x-48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"169\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66d0919d30c9defc68f93f5ee09d10d5e96700c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\  (2x+3)\\left(x^2+16\\right) \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\  (2x+3)(x+8)(x-8) \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\  2x\\left(x^2+3x-16\\right)+24 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\  (2x-3)(x-4)^2 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\  (2x+3)(x+4)(x-4) \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can group the terms like this:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd02f4d5b0523f5fbaa658e9237c1cce32b7d39b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2}(2x + 3) - 16(2x + 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"190\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b591f7ffa4c49f2719f1203a0815f656fda03c2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=(x^{2} - 16)(2x + 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Difference_of_squares\" title=\"Difference of squares\">difference of squares</a>:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/e/24e661370bbb0d33e0dd0b61268e0c25a9a1dcd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\boxed{\\textbf {(E) } (2x + 3)(x + 4)(x - 4)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"243\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/6/696f21f840b94ef83540a473b3ddfc8fbc0f281b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 2x^{3} + 3x^{2} - 32x - 48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"229\" height=\"21\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/0/380fda4cdea0e096423a66fe24959bf4e7bcf420.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(-4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"20\" />, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/4/48482ca390d1e3645f06fa4724a5a20d86d90889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times (-4)^{3} + 3 \\times (-4)^{2} - 32 \\times (-4) - 48 = 2 \\times -64 + 3 \\times 16 + 64 \\times 2 - 48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"588\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1ed0f1b58527ec6bf77b439253604eebaca0a89f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=48 - 48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Since this does equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72d85c6959aaabfff6e0104544ff25c1445f3f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" /> must be a root of the polynomial. Of the answer choices, the only one that has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72d85c6959aaabfff6e0104544ff25c1445f3f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" /> as a root is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/7/017cc9bec3e8f9e7fa6271d4c9a3be29321bcfb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(E) } (2x + 3)(x + 4)(x - 4)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"224\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest\">2025 TMTA Algebra I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b